uestion/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "68ba7826-02c2-5b69-a594-6dc133f00570" :question/math-academy-id "q-30923" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{x/3}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "If we let $u=\\frac{x}{3},$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{3}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nComputing our limits of integration, we get the following:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n\nThen, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{x/3}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{e}^{x/3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =({e}^{u}){|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & ={e}^{1}-{e}^{0} \\\\  & =e-1\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250122 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f4b340f6-0ac6-5bbf-a7d4-0088ca3c4e5e" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating the Exponential Function With a Linear Exponent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0609bfa0-feaa-5eb6-8746-b749fc1e9ec2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,{e}^{x-1}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247477} {:answer/id #uuid "253a16d7-628b-53f9-a7b2-1f6c746a4abb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\,{e}^{x/2\\,-\\,1}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247750} {:answer/id #uuid "2d6d85b6-5dd0-5f4b-aa63-52da5bb8cf45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,{e}^{x/2\\,-\\,1}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247828} {:answer/id #uuid "3bc85c63-a410-59bf-afe3-e5c1937a752b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{x/2\\,-\\,1}}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247953} {:answer/id #uuid "42a6cbcd-5218-511c-8178-7959687c4db1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x/2\\,-\\,1}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248018}] :answe